<title>UK: Natwest says to issue $300 mln ADRs.</title>
<headline>Natwest says to issue $300 mln ADRs.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's National Westminster Bank said on Wednesday that it would issue 12 million non-cumulative preference shares to raise $300 million.</p>
<p>The shares would have a nominal value of $25 each, to be represented by American Depositary Shares in the U.S., and will be listed on the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>The dividend rate will be determined on April 4.</p>
<p>Natwest said Merrill Lynch has been appointed as lead manager for the offering with Dean Witter Reynolds, AG Edwards &amp; Sons Inc, Paine Webber, Prudential Securities and Smith Barney as co-managers.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 5423 4366</p>
